            <td class="lt-chem-38322" data-th="Name" style="text-align:center;">carbonato</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="lt-chem-38322">When the complex is either a cation or a neutral molecule, the name of the central metal atom is spelled exactly like the name of the element and is followed by a Roman numeral in parentheses to indicate its oxidation state (Tables \(\PageIndex{2}\), \(\PageIndex{3}\), and \(\PageIndex{3}\)). When the complex is an anion, the suffix -ate is added to the stem of the name of the metal, followed by the Roman numeral designation of its oxidation state.</p>

